    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Some priests pride themselves on pragmatism. They understand that light casts a shadow, that darkness is defined by light, and that true discipline stems from one’s ability to balance these opposing powers in services of a greater cause. While these priests possess many holy virtues to aid their allies, they also dabble in the dark arts to debilitate their enemies.</p><h2>Discipline Calling Spells</h2><table><tbody><tr><td data-colwidth=\"53\"><p style=\"text-align:center\"><strong>Priest Level</strong></p></td><td><p style=\"text-align:center\"><strong>Spells</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"53\"><p style=\"text-align:center\">1st</p></td><td><p>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells.Item.uUWb1wZgtMou0TVP]{Cure Wounds}, @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells.Item.ksaaTxIbKx2sJfia]{Inflict Wounds}</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"53\"><p style=\"text-align:center\">3rd</p></td><td><p>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells.Item.5VhqFROQYjr1P9lp]{Silence}, @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells.Item.CylBa7jR8DSbo8Z3]{Zone of Truth}</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"53\"><p style=\"text-align:center\">5th</p></td><td><p>@UUID[Compendium.wc5e-foundryvtt.spells.Item.w4ylfjLx2L6xnwdo]{Divine Star}, @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells.Item.UfHQhA54M4323gVO]{Vampiric Touch}</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"53\"><p style=\"text-align:center\">7th</p></td><td><p>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells.Item.NJgxf7pmSsBArIG7]{Private Sanctum}, @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells.Item.1ADstb0Xec6HHRcU]{Resilient Sphere}</p></td></tr><tr><td data-colwidth=\"53\"><p style=\"text-align:center\">9th</p></td><td><p>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells.Item.TkJ8Wtg1L7TZtspm]{Dispel Evil and Good}, @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells.Item.o9ZCvuD2B1OTcubb]{Wall of Force}</p></td></tr></tbody></table>",
